<title>USA: TABLE - Mobile Mini Q2 results.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Mobile Mini Q2 results.</headline>
<dateline>TEMPE, Ariz. 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mobile Mini, Inc.</p>
<p>		   Condensed Statements of Operations</p>
<p>			  Three Months Ended	 Six Months Ended</p>
<p>				 June 30		     June 30</p>
<p>			 1997	    1996	  1997	   1996</p>
<p>Revenues   $12,193,795    $10,291,915 $21,843,251  $19,200,830</p>
<p>Net income before</p>
<p>extraordinary item</p>
<p>		  520,757	  322,714     722,519	208,746</p>
<p>Extraordinary item (1)</p>
<p>			 --		 --	    --     (410,354)</p>
<p>Net income (loss)</p>
<p>		 $520,757	 $322,714    $722,519    ($201,608)</p>
<p>Net income per common</p>
<p>and common share equivalent</p>
<p>before extraordinary item</p>
<p>		   $.08	     $.05	  $.11	   $.03</p>
<p>Extraordinary item (1)</p>
<p>		     --		 --	    --	  ($.06)</p>
<p>Net income (loss) per common</p>
<p>and common share equivalent</p>
<p>		   $.08	     $.05	  $.11	  ($.03)</p>
<p>Weighted average shares</p>
<p>outstanding</p>
<p>		6,739,324	6,739,324   6,739,324    6,735,841</p>
<p>(a): On March 29, 1996, the Company entered into a credit agreement with BT Commercial Corporation consisting of $35 million revolving line of credit and a $6 million term loan. In connection with the closing of the credit agreement, the Company terminated its existing credit line and repaid other long-term debt.  As a result, prepayment penalties and previously deferred costs related to certain indebtedness resulted in an extraordinary charge to earnings in the first quarter of 1996 of approximately $410,000, or $.06 per share, after the benefit for income taxes.</p>
